WEBVTT

00:00.421 --> 00:02.335
- [Instructor] Let's
see if we can calculate

00:02.335 --> 00:04.085
the fifth root of 32.

00:08.289 --> 00:10.412
So, like always, pause the
video and see if you can

00:10.412 --> 00:12.690
figure this out on your own.

00:12.690 --> 00:16.316
So, let's just remind
ourselves what a fifth root is.

00:16.316 --> 00:20.066
So, if x is equal to the fifth root of 32,

00:21.042 --> 00:22.551
that's the same thing as saying

00:22.551 --> 00:25.551
x to the fifth power is equal to 32.

00:27.612 --> 00:29.242
So, we have to find some number where,

00:29.242 --> 00:31.445
if you take five of them
and multiply them together,

00:31.445 --> 00:33.198
you'd get 32.

00:33.198 --> 00:35.400
So, there is a couple of
ways to approach this.

00:35.400 --> 00:36.749
Especially when you're dealing with these

00:36.749 --> 00:39.358
really high order roots here.

00:39.358 --> 00:43.108
So, let me rewrite the
fifth root of 32 here.

00:45.236 --> 00:47.805
One way is you could try to factor 32

00:47.805 --> 00:51.761
and see are there factors
that show up five times?

00:51.761 --> 00:54.655
So, 32 you might immediately
recognize is an even number.

00:54.655 --> 00:56.857
So, it's gonna be divisible by two.

00:56.857 --> 00:58.572
It's two times 16.

00:58.572 --> 01:00.405
16 is two times eight.

01:01.793 --> 01:03.793
Eight is two times four.

01:05.098 --> 01:07.300
Four is two times two.

01:07.300 --> 01:09.174
So, in this case, doing the

01:09.174 --> 01:10.881
factoring technique worked out well.

01:10.881 --> 01:12.310
'Cause we see that this is

01:12.310 --> 01:14.654
two times two times
two times two times two

01:14.654 --> 01:16.764
or two to the fifth power.

01:16.764 --> 01:19.257
You could rewrite this as the fifth root

01:19.257 --> 01:21.180
of two to the fifth power,

01:21.180 --> 01:24.198
which is, of course,
going to be equal to two.

01:24.198 --> 01:26.615
Two to the fifth power is 32.

01:29.584 --> 01:31.254
Now, let's do another one.

01:31.254 --> 01:34.763
It's gonna be a little bit harder.

01:34.763 --> 01:38.596
Let's say we wanna take
the fifth root of 243.

01:41.296 --> 01:43.747
So, now, a much, much larger number.

01:43.747 --> 01:45.261
So, there's a couple of ways to do this.

01:45.261 --> 01:47.262
One, you could try the factoring.

01:47.262 --> 01:48.363
Although, that's gonna be harder

01:48.363 --> 01:49.546
now that it's a larger number.

01:49.546 --> 01:52.034
Or you could do a little
bit of trial and error.

01:52.034 --> 01:54.969
Doing higher roots without the aid

01:54.969 --> 01:56.438
of some type of calculator or something

01:56.438 --> 01:59.536
is a little bit more complicated.

01:59.536 --> 02:02.921
So, here, if we wanted to
do the factoring technique.

02:02.921 --> 02:06.306
We could say, alright,
it's not divisible by two.

02:06.306 --> 02:08.557
I like to start with the
smallest possible factor.

02:08.557 --> 02:10.429
So, it's not divisible by two.

02:10.429 --> 02:12.466
Is it divisible by three?

02:12.466 --> 02:14.178
And you might be familiar with the test

02:14.178 --> 02:16.378
to see if something is divisible by three.

02:16.378 --> 02:18.253
You add up the digits and see if that

02:18.253 --> 02:20.822
sum of the digits is divisible by three.

02:20.822 --> 02:25.300
So, if I were to take
two plus four plus three,

02:25.300 --> 02:26.892
that is equal to nine.

02:26.892 --> 02:29.504
And so it is divisible by three.

02:29.504 --> 02:32.478
So, this is going to be
equal to three times...

02:32.478 --> 02:36.434
Let's see three goes into
240 80 times and then one.

02:36.434 --> 02:37.517
So, 81 times.

02:39.903 --> 02:42.392
And so, 81 is also divisible by three.

02:42.392 --> 02:45.123
I have a sense of where this is going now.

02:45.123 --> 02:49.810
It's three times 27,
which is three times nine.

02:49.810 --> 02:52.053
Which is three times three.

02:52.053 --> 02:53.403
So, using the factoring method,

02:53.403 --> 02:56.832
we're able to see that three
to the fifth power is 243.

02:56.832 --> 03:00.499
So, the fifth root of
243 is equal to three.

03:02.787 --> 03:04.335
Now, another way that
you could have done it

03:04.335 --> 03:06.213
is a little bit of trial and error.

03:06.213 --> 03:08.288
We already know..

03:08.288 --> 03:09.432
Well, we know that one to the fifth power

03:09.432 --> 03:10.938
is just going to be one.

03:10.938 --> 03:12.364
We know that two to the fifth power...

03:12.364 --> 03:13.382
We just calculated that.

03:13.382 --> 03:14.215
That's 32.

03:15.255 --> 03:17.254
Well, we now know what
three to the fifth is.

03:17.254 --> 03:18.191
Let's say we're just trying to

03:18.191 --> 03:20.068
zoom in on it a little bit.

03:20.068 --> 03:21.252
So, let's say, if you wanted to see

03:21.252 --> 03:23.496
what four to the fifth is.

03:23.496 --> 03:26.147
Well, that would be four times four

03:26.147 --> 03:28.583
times four times four times four.

03:28.583 --> 03:32.381
So, let's see, this is going to be 16.

03:32.381 --> 03:34.048
16 times four is 64.

03:37.029 --> 03:38.529
Times four is 256.

03:40.785 --> 03:42.585
And then, that times four...

03:42.585 --> 03:44.178
And I just happen to know this.

03:44.178 --> 03:46.460
But you might wanna do it by hand.

03:46.460 --> 03:47.543
This is 1024.

03:51.148 --> 03:53.682
So, if you're taking the cube root of 243,

03:53.682 --> 03:55.682
you're saying what to the fifth power...

03:55.682 --> 03:58.983
Something to the fifth
power is equal to 243.

03:58.983 --> 03:59.881
And, if you have a sense that

03:59.881 --> 04:02.043
it's going to be an integer solution,

04:02.043 --> 04:02.900
if you think it's going to be

04:02.900 --> 04:04.979
something like a two or a three,

04:04.979 --> 04:08.281
well, then, three is probably
going to be a good guess here.

04:08.281 --> 04:10.400
If the possible answers
are gonna be decimals,

04:10.400 --> 04:12.722
then it's going to be
a lot more complicated.

04:12.722 --> 04:13.621
But that's another way.

04:13.621 --> 04:15.007
Say, hey, maybe I'll try a three.

04:15.007 --> 04:18.757
And, if you try out
three, you would get 243.
